{
  "phase": "questions",
  "section": "document_intake",
  "questions": [
    "Do you have any existing documents to share (e.g., business requirements, system context, integration specs, data model notes, UI wireframes, or architecture diagrams) before we begin?"
  ],
  "summary": "You want help defining the high-level architecture for a new product called Scenarios. I will start with document intake to incorporate any existing materials before moving into structured discovery."
}

{
  "phase": "questions",
  "section": "artefact_review",
  "questions": [
    "Would you like to upload any additional artefacts (e.g., UI wireframes, API contracts for the webhook/promotion, or sequence diagrams) before I produce the consolidated architecture recap?"
  ],
  "summary": "Document received and analyzed. Coverage: context_and_boundaries (purpose, actors, hosting on GCP GKE EU West, OAuth2 via Google Cloud Identity, RBAC with two roles, internal-only, no mTLS) — COVERED; ui_and_channels (web micro-frontend via Module Federation + single-spa, embedded views, deep links, 5s polling, internal REST + inbound webhook) — COVERED; integrations (Market Data outbound GET/POST + inbound webhook with OAuth2 client credentials; FRTB SA & VaR REST reads; SSO via Google Identity) — COVERED; data_model (Cloud SQL for Postgres; Scenario/ChangeSet, ImpactSummary, ApprovalWorkflow, ApprovalDecision, Message/Comment, AuditEvent; external IDs; Postgres-only search) — COVERED; service_decomposition (single Spring Boot 3/Java 21 backend for MVP; React/TypeScript micro-frontend) — COVERED; business_logic (Scenario lifecycle; webhook-driven state advance; rules-based approvals; idempotent promotion with retries; comprehensive audit trail) — COVERED; non_functional (<50 users, ~10 concurrent, 99% availability, 7-year prod retention, basic Cloud Logging/Monitoring) — COVERED. Open items noted from your doc: approval rule definitions/schema/versioning; exact webhook and promotion API contracts; environment/network standards; RPO/RTO, backup/archival, non-prod retention; role-to-group mappings and any SoD constraints. Given the comprehensive coverage, I will skip detailed Q&A for covered sections and proceed to final review next after any optional artefact uploads."
}
